<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Magnus Maximus</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 335–388</span> · <a href="/centuries/4th-century">4th century</a> · Also known as Macsen Wledig</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Magnus Maximus was a Roman general of Spanish origin who, as commander in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>, was proclaimed emperor by his troops in 383. He crossed to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaul">Gaul</a>, where the emperor Gratian was killed, and ruled Britain, Gaul and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trier">Trier</a> until he invaded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> and was defeated and executed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theodosius-i">Theodosius I</a> in 388. In Welsh legend, as Macsen Wledig, he became an ancestor of several royal lines.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/magnus-maximus.jpg" alt="Magnus Maximus" width="320" height="299" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CNG · CC BY-SA 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rare_aureus_of_Magnus_Maximus_(obverse_transparent).png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
